<div class="instructions years">
  <p>We want to include information about  the experiment was performed. <strong>For multiple dates use the "Add More" button to add a form element for each one and do NOT use ranges.</strong></p>

  <dl>
    <dt>Field / Greenhouse / Growth Chamber</dt>
      <dd> Include the <strong>season and year</strong> for each time the field experiment was planted. For example, if you have both a summer and winter nursery you might enter "Summer 2024" and "Winter 2024" as dates below. Even if you only have a single growing season per year, it is still important to include the season.</dd>
    <dt>Biochemical Assay</dt>
      <dd>Provide the dates the experiment was conducted on. Provide as much granularity as possible using the formats <strong>YEAR-MONTH-DATE</strong> or <strong>YEAR-MONTH</strong>. For example, if you have the exact dates then you may enter "2024-March-10" and "2024-March-11" but if you do not know the days then you may have to resort to "2024-March".</dd>
  </dl>
</div>
